---
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
---
<Page
  title="Manifest"
  label="Tools"
  dek="Every Salvage tool: what it does, where it runs, and what it changes. The list is empty because nothing has shipped."
>
  <table class="ledger">
    <caption class="visually-hidden">Salvage tools</caption>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th scope="col">Tool</th>
        <th scope="col">Workstream</th>
        <th scope="col">What it does</th>
        <th scope="col">Soundings</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td colspan="4">Nothing has shipped yet.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>What goes on the manifest</h2>
    <p>A tool goes on this list when it has shipped and been measured. Each entry will say:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>What it does, in a sentence, and which workstream it belongs to.</li>
      <li>Which platforms and engine versions it has been tested on.</li>
      <li>Its <a href="/soundings/">soundings</a>: what it changed, measured before and after on named machines.</li>
      <li>How to remove it and put things back the way they were.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What's being looked at</h2>
    <h3>Lighter Unreal</h3>
    <p>
      Where Unreal Engine games and the editor spend memory, and how much of it the work actually needs. Memory comes
      first because it's the part of a machine that's hardest to afford right now.
    </p>
    <h3>Unreal on Mac</h3>
    <p>Where developing with Unreal Engine on macOS is slow or awkward, and what would make it fast and pleasant.</p>
    <p>
      Fixes that belong in the engine itself will go upstream to Epic Games as pull requests, so they won't appear on
      this list as tools. The <a href="/logbook/">logbook</a> will record them.
    </p>
  </div>
</Page>
<style>
  .ledger {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 62rem;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    margin-bottom: var(--s-4);
  }
  th {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    text-align: left;
    color: var(--muted);
    padding: 0 var(--s-4) var(--s-3) 0;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--text);
  }
  td {
    padding: var(--s-5) 0;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--rule);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--mark);
  }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    th:nth-child(3),
    th:nth-child(4) {
      display: none;
    }
  }
</style>
